abstract: >-
  Maple worksheets, MATLAB and Julia solvers, Mathematica notebooks and data for the quasinormal modes of massless
  scalar, electromagnetic and gravitational perturbations of Schwarzschild–de Sitter black holes, for dimensionless
  cosmological constants between 0.02 and 0.11, and of their Nariai limit. After the behaviour at the event and
  cosmological horizons is factored out, a Chebyshev collocation turns the radial problem into a quadratic eigenvalue
  problem, and only the roots on which three resolutions agree are kept; in the Nariai limit the computed frequencies
  are compared with the exact Pöschl–Teller spectrum.
